   "rationale": "The data are a Lorenz-type chaotic attractor contaminated by sparse impulsive outliers (spikes of ~40 units in about 0.5% of samples). These spikes corrupted the tool-based derivative fits, including weak SINDy. I despiked each series using a median-filter residual threshold, then estimated derivatives with Savitzky-Golay and ran STLSQ on a degree-2 polynomial library. Across windows 7/11/15 the same 7-term Lorenz structure was selected with stable coefficients: x'=a(y,x) linear, y'=c x - d y - e xz, z'=-b z + g xy. I refined the coefficients by robust multi-step shooting on the cleaned data, which changed them by <1%. Clean-data rollouts track the trajectories for ~1.4-2.8 time units, which is consistent with chaotic divergence. The validator's deriv_nrmse is inflated by the spikes in the held-out data.",
